-- title:
--   Hopf algebra structure on the n-torsion of a formal group
-- statement:
--   Let $\mathcal O$ be a commutative ring, $p$ a natural number, and assume $\mathcal O$ is separated and complete for the adic topology of the ideal $(p)$. Let $\Phi$ be a $d$-dimensional formal group law over $\mathcal O$, that is, a $d$-tuple $\Phi_i \in \mathcal O[[X_j, Y_j : j \in \mathrm{Fin}\,d]]$ (variables indexed by $\mathrm{Fin}\,d \sqcup \mathrm{Fin}\,d$) with vanishing constant terms, linear coefficients $\delta_{ij}$ in each of the two blocks, and satisfying the associativity identity under substitution; assume moreover `Φ.IsComm`, i.e. each $\Phi_i$ is invariant under interchanging the two blocks of variables. Fix $n$ and let $I = \mathrm{span}(\mathrm{range}\,(\Phi.\mathrm{nthSeries}\,n)) \subseteq \mathcal O[[X_1,\dots,X_d]]$, where `nthSeries` is defined recursively by $\mathrm{nthSeries}\,0 = 0$ and $\mathrm{nthSeries}\,(m+1)_i = \Phi_i(\mathrm{nthSeries}\,m, X)$, so that $I$ is generated by the components of the multiplication-by-$n$ series. Assume $\mathcal O[[X]]/I$ is free and finite as an $\mathcal O$-module, and that for each $i$ some power $X_i^N$ lies in $I + (p)$. Then there exist a type $L$ in the same universe, a commutative ring structure on it, a Hopf algebra structure over $\mathcal O$ whose comultiplication is cocommutative, freeness and finiteness of $L$ as an $\mathcal O$-module, and a surjective $\mathcal O$-algebra map $\pi : \mathcal O[[X_1,\dots,X_d]] \to L$ with $\ker \pi = I$, such that each $\pi(X_i)$ lies in the radical of the ideal $(p)$ of $L$; for every power series $G$, $\pi(G) = \mathrm{adicEval}$ of $G$ at the tuple $(\pi(X_i))_i$, the evaluation `MvPowerSeries.eval₂` along $\mathcal O \to L$ taken with respect to the $(p)$-adic topology on $L$ and the discrete uniformity on $\mathcal O$; for each $i$ the comultiplication satisfies $\Delta(\pi(X_i)) = \mathrm{adicEval}$ of $\Phi_i$ with respect to the ideal $(p)$ of $L \otimes_{\mathcal O} L$ at the tuple sending the $j$-th variable of the first block to $\pi(X_j) \otimes 1$ and of the second block to $1 \otimes \pi(X_j)$; and the counit satisfies $\varepsilon(\pi(G)) = G(0)$, the constant coefficient of $G$.
--
--   This realises the kernel of multiplication by $n$ on $\Phi$ as a finite locally free commutative group scheme over $\mathcal O$: the quotient $\mathcal O[[X]]/([n]_\Phi)$ is exhibited as the coordinate ring of $\Phi[n]$, with comultiplication induced by the group law and counit given by evaluation at the origin. It is used in the study of the $n$-torsion of formal groups, and is cited by [`MvFormalGroup.exists_add_le_and_forall_exists_sub_sum_smul_mem_span_nthSeries_of_addCoboundary_mem_span`](thm.html#MvFormalGroup.exists_add_le_and_forall_exists_sub_sum_smul_mem_span_nthSeries_of_addCoboundary_mem_span).
